1
00:00:00,512 --> 00:00:08,792
Workbench now searches the entire collection by name, notes, or storage location.
This demonstration uses synthetic

2
00:00:08,792 --> 00:00:11,380
records in a disposable database.

3
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:19,596
Type a remembered phrase and press Search. Matching ignores letter case and treats
punctuation literally. Here,

4
00:00:19,596 --> 00:00:26,392
September fair appears in the notes, so the sapphire is found even though its name is

5
00:00:26,392 --> 00:00:26,817
different.

6
00:00:28,236 --> 00:00:35,268
On a phone, choose the compact list and open the sapphire. Its location is right
here.

7
00:00:35,268 --> 00:00:42,299
Returning to the collection preserves the query, list view, and selected result.
Changing appearance keeps the

8
00:00:42,299 --> 00:00:43,178
task intact.

9
00:00:44,589 --> 00:00:51,703
A simulated connection failure shows an error, not an empty collection. Retry repeats
the submitted query

10
00:00:51,703 --> 00:00:53,927
and retrieves the matching piece.

11
00:00:55,339 --> 00:01:01,294
A phrase with no matches has its own message. Clear returns to the collection without
changing

12
00:01:01,294 --> 00:01:07,249
any records. Search state stays in this signed-in app and resets on a full reload or

13
00:01:07,249 --> 00:01:07,621
sign-out.
